{"name":"Grandmother’s Pantry","hex":"#644847","fetched":"2026-10-18","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"grandmother","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A mother of someone's parent.","A female ancestor or progenitor."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grandmother"},{"term":"pantry","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A small room, closet, or cabinet usually located in or near the kitchen, dedicated to shelf-stable  food storage or storing kitchenware, like a larder, but smaller.","A break room."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pantry"}],"entries":[{"title":"Pantry","blocks":[{"text":"A pantry is a room or cupboard where beverages, food, (sometimes) dishes, household cleaning products, linens or provisions are stored within a home or office. Food and beverage pantries serve in an ancillary capacity to the kitchen."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/04/Residential-pantry.jpg/330px-Residential-pantry.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pantry","wikidata":"Q258313"},{"title":"Grandparent","blocks":[{"text":"Grandparents, individually known as grandmother and grandfather, or Grandma and Grandpa, are the parents of a person's father or mother – paternal or maternal. Every sexually reproducing living organism who is not a genetic chimera has a maximum of 4 genetic grandparents, 8 genetic great-grandparents, 16 genetic great-great-grandparents, 32 genetic great-great-great-grandparents, 64 genetic great-great-great-great-grandparents, etc. In the history of modern humanity, around 30,000 years ago, the number of modern humans who lived to be a grandparent increased. It is not known for certain what spurred this increase in longevity, but it is generally believed that a key consequence of three generations being alive together was the preservation of information which could otherwise have been lost; an example of this important information might have been where to find water in times of drought."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b2/The_Favorite_by_Georgios_Iakovidis.jpg/330px-The_Favorite_by_Georgios_Iakovidis.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grandparent","wikidata":"Q167918"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/04/Residential-pantry.jpg/500px-Residential-pantry.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/04/Residential-pantry.jpg/1280px-Residential-pantry.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/04/Residential-pantry.jpg/500px-Residential-pantry.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A contemporary kitchen pantry","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AResidential-pantry.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/24/Museu_Rom%C3%A0ntic_Can_Papiol_%28Vilanova_i_la_Geltr%C3%BA%29_-_8.jpg/500px-Museu_Rom%C3%A0ntic_Can_Papiol_%28Vilanova_i_la_Geltr%C3%BA%29_-_8.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/24/Museu_Rom%C3%A0ntic_Can_Papiol_%28Vilanova_i_la_Geltr%C3%BA%29_-_8.jpg/1280px-Museu_Rom%C3%A0ntic_Can_Papiol_%28Vilanova_i_la_Geltr%C3%BA%29_-_8.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/24/Museu_Rom%C3%A0ntic_Can_Papiol_%28Vilanova_i_la_Geltr%C3%BA%29_-_8.jpg/500px-Museu_Rom%C3%A0ntic_Can_Papiol_%28Vilanova_i_la_Geltr%C3%BA%29_-_8.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Nineteenth-century pantry in Museu Romàntic Can Papiol in Vilanova i la Geltrú","l